        "original_id": "bde213b3-6ac8-5f08-963b-02208e9b4f7b",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Songs: \"Pinball Wizard\", \"Overture\", \"Underture\", \"Sparks\"\n- Albums: \"Tommy\"\n- People: The Who\n- Topics: chart performance, album release, instrumental tracks\n\nFacts:\n- The Who first released the double album \"Tommy\" in May 1969 as the band's fourth studio album.\n- The original recording of \"Pinball Wizard\" was released as a single in 1969 and reached No. 4 on the UK charts and No. 19 on the U.S. Billboard Hot 100.\n- \"Overture\" is one of three instrumental tracks on \"Tommy\", alongside \"Underture\" and \"Sparks\".\n- \"Overture\" includes some lyrics toward the end despite being one of the instrumental tracks on \"Tommy\".",
